    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "Candidate 5 (STANDARD) is the most likely to succeed because it employs a highly professional, standard, and respectful tone while comprehensively addressing all statutory and procedural requirements. It successfully executes the preemptive formalities curing by filing a Substitute Specification to excise embedded elements, which preserves the license grant and complies with 37 CFR 1.125. Furthermore, it perfectly implements the mathematically optimized fee allocation knapsack strategy under 37 CFR 1.22(b) to prevent stranded funds, and correctly requests the transfer of the $1,440 overpayment to the deposit account. The language is clear, deferential ('respectfully requests', 'Pursuant to'), and avoids the unnecessary assertiveness or irrelevant portfolio-wide grievances found in other candidates.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": null,
    "ats_alignment_assessment": "All candidates align well with the ATS brief by addressing the Notice to File Missing Parts, curing the 37 CFR 1.63 declaration defect, and implementing the exact Path B fee allocation knapsack strategy. They also all successfully execute the highly rewarded preemptive Substitute Specification filing. Candidate 5 stands out for its optimal stylistic alignment with USPTO norms.",
